# Build context is the repository root. Everything here is either unusable in
# the image, or actively harmful to ship into one.
#
# The .venv exclusion is the one that matters most: it is a full local
# virtualenv built for this host, hundreds of megabytes, and it would be sent
# to the daemon on every build only to be overwritten by the one uv builds.

# --- virtualenvs and caches ---
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- version control and editors ---
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- secrets: the image takes its configuration from the environment ---
# .env.example is kept: it is documentation, not configuration.
.env
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# --- runtime state, regenerated in the container ---
logs/
**/logs/
src/assets/
**/qdrant_db/

# --- not part of the application ---
test/
Docker/
skills/
README.md
LICENSE
pytest.ini
*.md

# Anything named like a virtualenv, at any depth: a set-aside broken one
# (src/.venv.broken-intxlnk, 1 GB) matched none of the patterns above, was
# uploaded as build context on every build, and was then copied into the
# image by `COPY src/`.
**/.venv*/
# Tool caches below the root as well as at it (src/.mypy_cache was 290 MB).
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# The image reads only src/ (see the Dockerfile's COPY and bind mounts), so the
# rest of the repository is never sent: tests, evaluation, the demo and its
# recording assets, diagrams, notebooks.
tests/
evals/
demo/
docs/
scripts/
software_engineering/
fineTuning/
colabNotebooks/
.claude/
.github/
.githooks/
